Experience the perfect combination of comfort, security, independence, and modern living in this brand-new NDIS SDA Robust home at 19 Aeolus Street, Armstrong Creek. Purpose-built to meet Specialist Disability Accommodation (SDA) standards, this thoughtfully designed residence provides a safe and supportive environment while offering contemporary style and quality finishes throughout.



Situated in one of Victoria's fastest-growing communities, this home delivers convenient access to local amenities, healthcare services, shopping centres, public transport, and recreational facilities, making everyday living easier and more enjoyable.



Key Features

Brand new NDIS SDA Robust compliant home

Designed to support participant independence and quality of life

Modern single-level floorplan with accessible living spaces

Spacious open-plan living and dining area

Contemporary kitchen with quality appliances

Generous bedrooms with built-in storage

Wide hallways and circulation spaces

Accessible bathroom facilities

Secure and durable construction throughout

Low-maintenance landscaped grounds

Private outdoor living area

Dedicated on-site support provisions (subject to SDA design requirements)

Energy-efficient design and fixtures

Secure neighbourhood in a growing community



Other Features

Reverse-cycle air conditioning

Modern LED lighting throughout

Quality flooring finishes

Roller blinds included

Ample storage solutions

Fully fenced property

Secure entry points

NBN-ready connectivity

Water-efficient fixtures

Contemporary façade with attractive street appeal

Easy-care gardens and lawns

Concrete driveway and pathways



Home Design



Designed with both functionality and comfort in mind, this brand-new SDA Robust residence features a practical layout that promotes accessibility, independence, and daily living support.



The home incorporates:



Open-plan living, dining, and kitchen zones

Spacious bedrooms designed for comfort and accessibility

Wide doorways and circulation areas

Durable finishes suitable for robust accommodation requirements

Functional bathroom layouts

Secure and private outdoor spaces

Natural light throughout the home

Modern architecture with a welcoming street presence



Every aspect of the design has been carefully considered to create a safe, comfortable, and contemporary home environment for eligible SDA participants.





Quality kitchen cabinetry

Stone benchtops

Stainless steel appliances

Electric cooktop and oven

Dishwasher

Split-system air conditioning

Built-in wardrobes

Modern bathroom fixtures and fittings

Durable wall and flooring finishes

Security screens where applicable

LED downlights throughout

Landscaping and fencing completed

Rainwater-saving features

Energy-efficient hot water system

NBN connection readiness

Location Highlights



Located in the thriving Armstrong Creek growth corridor, this property offers excellent access to essential services and lifestyle amenities.



Nearby conveniences include:



Armstrong Creek Town Centre

